 Text:RFD2495  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-14T00:00:56Z (RFD66606-2495) '- The GarmentCode segmentation file has one label per vertex of the box mesh: 29,667 labels
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2495  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-14T00:00:57Z (RFD66606-2495) '  and 29,667 vertices for one garment. The draped mesh has 29,784 vertices. Matching by index
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2495  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-14T00:00:58Z (RFD66606-2495) '  gives 83.2 percent of faces whose non-seam vertices share one panel, against 12.3 percent
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2495  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-14T00:00:59Z (RFD66606-2495) '  for a shuffled control. Exact labels on a drape need a drape we run ourselves.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2495  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-14T00:01:00Z (RFD66606-2495) '- Seam vertices are 4.6 percent of batch 0.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2495  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-14T00:01:01Z (RFD66606-2495) '- RF-DETR segmentation fine-tuned on Fashionpedia, a local clothing set and pseudo-labelled
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2495  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-14T00:01:02Z (RFD66606-2495) '  poseswap garments matched the baseline on held-out photographs: mask AP 0.327 against 0.328
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2495  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-14T00:01:03Z (RFD66606-2495) '  on the test split. Pseudo-labels added edges, not knowledge.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2495  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-14T00:01:04Z (RFD66606-2495) '- Segment ran on its README example in 6 to 12 seconds and 10.5 GB of GPU memory. Its labels
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2495  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-14T00:01:05Z (RFD66606-2495) '  come from MeanShift clustering of the colours it paints, so they are anonymous same-part
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2495  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-14T00:01:06Z (RFD66606-2495) '  ids, not class ids.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2495  1 LINE
 Text:Written

